      "text": "SohoPay onboarding is only partly done. This agent is registered but **cannot pay merchants yet**, because your account has no wallet or bank account connected.\n\n**Done**\n- **Agent registration:** `operational_agent_id` is `oa_7910c05c88e34916` and `terminal_id` is `term_19495d063daf7ccf`.\n- **Borrower:** `583bbb05-6f05-4cb3-ba6c-7e4de5b9a4ca`, status ACTIVE.\n- **Handle:** `@agentbbe21a` was already claimed, so I didn't claim another.\n- **Token:** I received a token (900 s lifetime) with `payment:read`, `credit:facility:accept` and `handle:claim`.\n\n**Not done**\n- **Spend scopes:** the token came back without `spend:intent:create`, `policy:evaluate` and `signing:request`, reason `WALLET_PROOF_REQUIRED`. This is expected for an account signed in by phone.\n- **Workload key and agent grant:** I skipped both. The grant can't be made until a wallet is connected, so the key would have no use yet.\n- **Wallet proof:** I didn't ask for a signature, since there is no wallet to sign with.\n- **Authorization-context call (step 7):** I skipped it. It's a raw HTTP endpoint and I have no tool or base URL for it in this session.\n\n**What you need to do**\n1. Open the browser handoff for `CONNECT_WALLET` or `CONNECT_BANK`. I wasn't given a URL for it, so you'll need to start it from your SohoPay account. Your credit evaluation (`NOT_EVALUATED`) also runs after one of these is connected.\n2. Tell me once that's done. I'll then run the wallet proof, token refresh, workload key and agent grant, and the account will be ready to pay."
